Nit (low likelihood):
If a (kv-cache dtype, query dtype) group ends up with only the f16 MFMA arm, for example after the fp8-MFMA variants are dropped from VARIANTS, then ordered == ["f16"]. Its first and only arm is then emitted as a bare else { right after if (query.dtype() == ...) {. The generator succeeds and the failure only shows up later as a C++ syntax error in attention_dispatch.cu. I reproduced it by filtering VARIANTS:

    else if (kv_cache_dtype == "fp8" || kv_cache_dtype == "fp8_e4m3") {
     if (query.dtype() == at::ScalarType::Half) {
         else {

   A lone f16 arm is the catch-all anyway, so it can take the no-split path:

               if mfma_types in ([None], ["f16"]):
                   lines.extend(block_size_switch(by_mfma[mfma_types[0]], 6))

   This keeps the SystemExit for a group without an f16 arm.

